Committed. Here's what happened.

## The defect

collect_failed_ci_fingerprints called gh run list --status failure --limit 5 with no date filter — the five most recent failures ever — and rendered them under a header claiming "(failed runs in window)". createdAt was already being fetched and discarded.

Measured today: no failed run in 4 days, last 10 sessions 2/2 green, and two of the five fingerprints are the setup::tests::test_wizard_* panics that #780's chdir removals already cured. Resolved history, handed to my planner as current state.

## What I built (`scripts/extract_trajectory.py`, one file)

• `run_age_days(created_at, now)` — pure; None for missing/unparseable, deliberately never 0.0.
• `partition_failed_runs(runs, now, window_days)` — pure; three states (in_window / too_old / undated), none folded into another. Undated is counted and reported.
• Filter runs before the gh run view --log-failed loop, so it also saves the slow calls.
• Clusters carry newest-run age → `[2×, last 4d ago] …; header names the window. Reuses the existing WINDOW_DAYS`.
• render_ci_errors takes a CiScan, giving its three worlds separate sentences — plus a fourth I found while writing it: runs are in window but every log fetch died, which now reports unreadable logs instead of "clean".
• The could-not-check line isn't counted as trajectory data in main, so it can't suppress the global (no trajectory data yet) state.

## Verification

• python3 scripts/extract_trajectory.py --test → ALL PASSED, 17 new cases including both sides of the boundary (exactly 14d inside, 14d+1min outside).
• cargo fmt --check, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, build, test — all green (no Rust changed).
• Real run against this repo: the clean branch correctly does not fire — all five failures are 3–4 days old and genuinely inside the 14-day window. The visible change today is the age labels and the window-named header, exactly as the task predicted. I didn't tune the window until it read "clean".

CLAUDE.md's extract_trajectory.py bullet updated with the age filter, the three render states, and the reason.
